# Power Bay — photo selection manifest
# Lists ONLY the shots we keep, and what each becomes in the guide.
# Format:  SOURCE   target.webp      (# comments + blank lines ignored)
# Convert with (any OS — needs `pip install pillow pillow-heif`):
#   python3 tools/convert_build_photos.py <staging-dir> docs/assets/build/power-bay/photos.manifest docs/assets/build/power-bay
# That holds every output under the 300 KB target in docs/assets/build/README.md.
#
# Source: the "5 - Power Bay Build" Drive folder, which groups shots into
# sub-folders by PROCESS rather than numbering them across the whole build. Only
# "1 Back Plate Screw Mount" carries an explicit number; the rest of the order
# below is inferred from the photos themselves — each process starts from the
# state the previous one ended in. See the note in docs/build/power-bay.md.
#
# Source folder names are kept verbatim on the left (typos and trailing spaces
# included, since that is what is on Drive); the targets fix them.

